{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "bi8Au",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Admin / Brief / Happy path band",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 22,
      "padding": 36,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a3lK0",
          "name": "Flow title",
          "fill": "$on-surface",
          "content": "Admin — the operator's dashboard",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tYURy",
          "name": "Kit pin",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "content": "kit-version-source 0.3.0 · band 1 of 2 · happy path · 6 of 6 screens drawn",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "XiA6X",
          "name": "Purpose",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "m1I82",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Purpose",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z30eK",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Sign in is the front door — the screen an installed dashboard shows every time the 12-hour session ends, and the only one that must render when the rest of the admin cannot. Behind it, five pages sit under one sidebar, read left to right in nav order. Overview answers what is failing, how much headroom is left, what is running now, how slow it is, what it cost and what traffic looked like. Request Logs is where the operator lives — every Overview error row links into it, pre-filtered. API Keys is who may call and what they spent. Playground sends a real request through the real /v1 path with a real key. System is what is running and which providers are allowed to answer.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ySQXf",
          "name": "Entry points",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PcPRv",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Entry points",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lt8bE",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "/admin/login — the sign-in page, src/admin/login.js, where every unauthenticated request lands; its next parameter returns the operator to the tab the session died on. /admin/dashboard/ — Overview is the default page; the five sidebar items are src/admin/public/js/app.js:209. Two real transitions exist and both are drawn as destinations: Overview → Logs via openErrorLogs(), which puts a filter in the nav store before setting location.hash, and API Keys → Logs via openKeyLogs().",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "s7ZA9",
          "name": "Screens in this band",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "CQ2Jw",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Screens in this band",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vbl2W",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Six screens, all at dac0bc6: Sign in / Default, Overview / Default, Request Logs / Default, API Keys / Default, Playground / Answered, System / Default. Two carry an expanded sub-state rather than a screen of their own — Logs shows its third row expanded (where request_id, upstream status and the cache counters live) and API Keys shows its third key in edit (where the 'rotate replaces the secret' rule is stated). Playground is drawn answered rather than idle, because the idle state is one sentence ('Nothing sent yet.') and the answered state is the layout. Overview alone carries the 1440×900 fold marker (grid-fold-y): it is the only screen whose content runs past the declared frame, so it is the only one where the fold falls inside something.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "gskz5",
          "name": "Business rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UrSK7",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Business rules",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "maNao",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One window everywhere a figure is aggregated: every request the pruner has not deleted, bounded at 30 days. No period selector — removed 2026-09-20. Overview's two charts share one time axis from the oldest surviving request to just past now; quiet hours are zero, not skipped. Logs paginates server-side (25/50/100) and its two panels read that same window, which is why they no longer claim '60m' or 'today'. API Keys reports usage over its own 7d window, set server-side and printed in the column header. Playground authenticates like any other caller — same key, same rate limit, same log row — and deliberately does not use apiFetch, so a 401 there reads as a refused client key rather than an expired admin session. Pausing a provider on System takes it out of routing; it does not sign it out.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "otdq2",
          "name": "Copy source",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MqB2L",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Copy source",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "F7BCS8",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "src/admin/views/pages/*.html verbatim, plus index.html for the shell and src/admin/login.js for Sign in. Numbers are illustrative; every label, verdict sentence, note and empty-state string is the code's. Timestamps render in SHELLM_TZ, default America/Mexico_City. The logo is mirrored from logo-dark.svg, which is SVG text rather than artwork: '>_ ' in mono, 'She' and 'M' in white, 'LL' in primary-container. Sign in ships its own self-contained <style> and sets everything in the mono stack — it shares no stylesheet with the dashboard, which is D20.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "P2Kx9l",
          "name": "States not drawn",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ia1G8",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "States not drawn",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "anChz",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The states this band leaves out are drawn in band 2 below, which exists now: Sign in's 401 and 429, the Playground's three catalog states and its waiting clock, the degraded banner, USAGE LIMIT HIT, and the unreachable or genuinely-empty states on Overview, Logs, Keys and System. That band's brief lists what it still leaves as a string swap, with the copy. What is not drawn here is only what the canvas cannot hold: two of Sign in's four CRT layers are repeating patterns it cannot tile — a 40px dot grid and a 1px/3px line texture — and they carry a CRT TEXTURE NOT MIRRORED note on the artboard with their values and timings. Overview's two chart interiors ARE drawn, from production captures plus the Chart.js config: axes, grid, colours, the dashed now marker and the mark geometry are the code's, and the marks plot this screen's illustrative dataset, not the captures'.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "E1ghK",
          "name": "Open findings",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dGbav",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Open findings",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NgWjW",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "D18 · D20 remain. D45 is closed: the 36 nodes drawing text-sm at 13px and the 4 drawing text-lg at 17 moved to $text-sm and $text-lg, together with the 16 the error band inherited — 52 and 8 in all. The Logs table's 25 fixed-width cells were checked before the change and again after; nothing wrapped and no artboard moved. The 5 thirteens on Sign in were left alone, because login.js sets .8rem there and they were always right. D46 opened and closed the same day, in band 2 where drawing it is what found it: System's Concurrency card rendered zeros for a health read that never happened, and now renders the em dash Overview always used. D20 stays visible on the canvas — Sign in is drawn from its own nine aliases, pinned to the canonical values by a test, and the kit is not asked to pretend otherwise. D16, D43, D15, D17 and D19 all closed 2026-09-20. One kit gap surfaced here and is still NOT fixed in the kit: the sweep gradient needs a fully transparent stop, so #03e3ff00 remains the only hex in this flow.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "rcUef",
          "name": "History",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "DrLYe",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "History",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "i5s6h",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "See the Log frame below this band.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
