    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "s6IUse",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4968,
      "name": "Log",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container-low",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 12,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j9t2ZO",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$primary-container",
          "content": "LOG",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SYdMB",
          "name": "2026-09-20l",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · The first fidelity loop this flow has actually run, and it earned its keep. The band was drawn from the code, then checked against the app in a browser — the service worker serving its cached shell for the dead-gateway states, a fake CLI on PATH for the waiting clock, no subscription quota spent. Four screens were wrong. System drew 'Latest release unknown — could not reach GitHub', which that screen cannot render: fetchLatestRelease returns early when the build is unknown (system.js:99-101), so releaseError is never set. That is invented copy — the one failure this method exists to prevent — and three readings of the file had not caught it. Logs drew Export CSV and Clear All, both x-show total > 0 and so hidden at zero. The three never-answered screens drew a read timestamp in the banner, the header and the footer; lastReadAt is written only by a read that succeeded, so all of them go and those footers are the product name alone. Sign in drew a filled password field against a server that re-renders it empty. The Playground catalog failure is now a 500, because /admin/providers has no 503 path — 503 is /v1's. Kept on purpose: the Keys activity log stays expanded, one click from its default, because its empty line renders nowhere else.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "F6rPN",
          "name": "2026-09-20k",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · D46 closed in code the same day the drawing opened it. System's Concurrency card now guards Running, Waiting and Streams on healthRead === 'ok' and renders the em dash Overview always used; Open circuits guards on the providers read instead, because openCircuits filters this.providers and not health — guarding it on the health read would have hidden a genuinely open circuit while the providers read was fine. Four tests pin it and the load-bearing one asserts that a never-answered read and a genuine zero can never render alike. Admin / System / Unreachable is re-drawn to the fixed behaviour: four em dashes where it drew the zeros, which is the only reason it drew them. This Log is also reordered newest-first here — design/README.md always said newest first and eleven entries had drifted the other way.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ikVgX",
          "name": "2026-09-20j",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Drew band 2, the error band, and closed D45. Nine screens: the two sign-in panels D43 left behind, Overview not-updating and usage-limit, Logs unreachable, Keys empty, Playground waiting and no-provider, System unreachable. Every string was copied from the code and none written for the canvas — the band's subject is copy, not layout, so eight of the nine are a band 1 artboard with the failing slot swapped. Three also change the shell, which the happy path never shows: a failed health poll puts UNREACHABLE in the sidebar and drops the footer's uptime. D45 closed in the same session, the one that could finally see what it drew: 52 nodes to $text-sm and 8 to $text-lg, the Logs table's 25 fixed-width cells checked before and again after, zero wrapped and zero artboards moved. The 17 thirteens on the three Sign in artboards stay — login.js really does set .8rem. D46 came out of the drawing rather than a read: System's Concurrency card reports zeros for a health read that never happened, while the sidebar beside it says UNREACHABLE.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Dyzwt",
          "name": "2026-09-20i",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Vendored kit 0.3.0 — the twenty-one type, icon and spacing tokens D35 and D39 asked for. Nothing renders differently from installing them; two things do render differently from applying them. The four latency figures, the Logs error rate and its two totals were drawn at 26px against the code's text-2xl, which is 24, and the page footer was 9px on five screens after the code collapsed it to 10 (fa9a87d). Both fixed, both now pointing at $text-2xl and $text-label rather than a number. What is NOT fixed is logged as D45: the canvas draws text-sm as 13 in 36 places and text-lg as 17 in 4, and correcting a size in a fixed-width table cell without being able to look at the result is how a mirror pass introduces the overflow it exists to catch.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "IyKEQ",
          "name": "2026-09-20h",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Drew both chart interiors, which this flow had refused to draw since it was created. What changed is the evidence: production captures of the shipped scatter and timeline exist now, and a capture outranks a guess in the source-of-truth order — the refusal was never about charts, it was about inventing one. The chrome is the code's, read from the Chart.js config rather than from the picture: grid rgba(132,147,151,0.1), which over surface-container is exactly surface-container-high, so the canvas uses the token; status-ok / status-warn / status-fail per point; pointRadius 3; status-ok-fill under the requests line; both charts on one time domain with the dashed now marker at 97% and a 'now' label in 10px mono. The captures' own tick labels were NOT copied — they read '02:33 PM' and '2026-09-19 20:00', and the shipped formatter is hourCycle h23 with formatDayHour only past 36h, so the axes read 13:02 … 07:47. The marks plot this screen's illustrative dataset (107 requests, 91 ok and 16 4xx clustered in the last hour, p50 1.4s against a tail to 19s) rather than the captures' seven requests at 100% ok, which would have contradicted every table on the page. The timeline plot is 180px, which is what the code says; it had been drawn at 200.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j4AA6R",
          "name": "2026-09-20g",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-mirrored against dac0bc6 after ten commits moved the views, and drew Sign in / Default — the band is 6 of 6. The code led on that screen and on the CRT treatment, which inverts the source-of-truth rule deliberately (D30, PEN-TODO). Applied in the flow: card titles and section eyebrows are now two levels, 19 nodes moved to on-surface-variant without tracking; Errors sits below Now, because the drawn state has no 5xx and order-1 is Now; the Errors table reports Model, not Route; the second quota window reads Last 18h with the burn rate divided by the hours that actually happened (B5) and the verdict it now renders; the Overview meta row carries '· read'; the Logs summary band moved above the table and onto surface-container without the brand rail. grid-fold-y = 900 is declared and marked on Overview only — the other five screens are shorter than the fold. Not fixed here: the sweep needs a transparent gradient stop the kit has no token for, so #03e3ff00 is the one hex in this flow.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XboKn",
          "name": "2026-09-20f",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-vendored at kit 0.2.0. The four UNTOKENISED locals are gone: D19 gave three of them names in the code (surface-shell, nav-selected, danger-surface) and the fourth is Tailwind's own white, which the markup uses 38 times. 58 nodes repointed, then read back — zero references to a local and zero dangling token references. The suffix did its job: it made the next re-vendor surface them instead of letting them pass as if the kit had always had them.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DNDoU",
          "name": "2026-09-20e",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Re-mirrored after the audit close-out landed in code. Overview's queue panel gained the age of the oldest in-flight request and the quota window gained a burn verdict read against the week; System's circuit lines gained a verdict that says what the state costs and what ends it. Two things were drawn and then removed rather than kept: an empty auth verdict, which a healthy provider does not render, and Playground's waiting row, which would have claimed the answer arrived while the page was still waiting. Both are now in states-not-drawn with the reason.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GEslu",
          "name": "2026-09-20d",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Added API Keys / Default (third key in edit), Playground / Answered and System / Default. Band complete at 5 of 5. The sidebar is built by one function per screen rather than copied and patched, and every screen is now read back to assert exactly one nav item is active — the check that would have caught the two-highlight bug before Adrian did. One overflow found and fixed by reading bounds on API Keys: the fixed column widths left the Actions cell 68px for three buttons.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iuYJg",
          "name": "2026-09-20c",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Sidebar rebuilt after Adrian caught two defects in it. It had an invented text wordmark where the code loads logo-dark.svg; that file is pure SVG text, so it is now mirrored exactly — '>_ ' in mono, 'She' and 'M' in white, 'LL' in primary-container. Nav labels were sentence case at 13px and are uppercase at 11px with 1.65 tracking, matching font-headline uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[0.6875rem]. Every item now carries the 4px left border the code gives all of them (transparent when inactive), so labels no longer shift between states. The bottom row (UP uptime + docs, sign-out and GitHub links) and the page footer were missing entirely; 'last read' had been put in the sidebar, where it does not live — it belongs to the degraded banner in main, which is conditional and not drawn. Second defect: Request Logs showed two active nav items, because Update({fill: undefined}) does not clear a fill, it ignores the key. Both sidebars are now built by one function that sets every item explicitly, active or not, and a read-back asserts exactly one is active per screen.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VWK6z",
          "name": "Findings note",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "D19 grew by two while mirroring the sidebar: #3b1a1a (Clear All background) and #ffffff (the logo, and text-white throughout the markup). Pure white is not on the palette — on-surface is #e0e3e7.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I38f1",
          "name": "2026-09-20b",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Added Admin / Request Logs / Default with its third row expanded. Sidebar copied from Overview and re-pointed rather than rebuilt. Two overflows found and fixed by reading bounds, not by looking: the filter row's fixed select widths left the action group no room, and a sparkline bar was taller than the box that clips it. One more untokenised colour surfaced — #3b1a1a, the Clear All background — now flow-local under D19. Mirrored after the Logs panels stopped claiming 'Last 60m' and 'Today' for a figure that covers the whole retained window.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "d2lYIx",
          "name": "2026-09-20",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Flow created from the blank starter. Vendored kit 0.1.1 (37 variables: the kit's 34, kit-version-source, plus shell-surface-UNTOKENISED and nav-active-UNTOKENISED held flow-local because the kit has no name for them — see D19). Mirrored Admin / Overview / Default against src/admin/views/pages/overview.html at 6cfefe0, after the period selector was removed and both charts moved onto one time axis. Two token values were found invalid while vendoring: status-ok-fill and overlay-scrim were stored as rgba(), which the .pen schema does not accept. Fixed in both files; the kit bumped to 0.1.1.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
